Package: displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-kwin
Architecture: any
Depends: kwin-wayland (= ${binary:Version}), libkwin6 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: displayxr-window-geometry-publisher,
          displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-kwin,
Conflicts: displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-kwin,
Replaces: displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-kwin,
Description: DisplayXR window-geometry service for KWin
 A KWin plugin that serves org.displayxr.WindowGeometry on the session bus:
 the position, size and output of every normal window, with the output's
 scale, so that a spatial display runtime (DisplayXR's, or a vendor's) can
 weave a lenticular or other phase-sensitive picture where the window's
 pixels are. It also moves a client's own window on request, keeps a window
 the user drags on the positions the client's drag table allows or paints it
 where each frame was woven for (move sync), and keeps a client's own
 windows out of screenshots and screen casts.
 .
 Any program on the session bus can read the titles and rectangles of the
 windows, as with the GNOME Shell extension that serves the same interface.
 KWin loads the plugin when it starts, so it takes effect at the next login;
 it is turned off with displayxrEnabled=false in the [Plugins] group of
 kwinrc.
